  "question": {
    "text": "For some <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> if the eccentricity of the hyperbola, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math> times the&nbsp;eccentricity of the ellipse, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the length of the latus rectum of the ellipse, is",
